0106_screening_baseline_backfill — NOT CARRIED AS A STEP, BECAUSE THERE ARE NO ROWS TO CORRECT.

The shared entry backfills `account_settings.screening_baseline_at` for accounts that consented
while the baseline was stamped only alongside a window. Those rows exist because the shared
journal has been running in production since mail 0056.

This journal has never shipped, so no store in the world holds a row written by the old door. A
device store is created by the baseline and then by the doors as they are today, which stamp the
baseline at consent whether or not a window came with it — the state this backfill repairs is
unreachable here.

WHAT CHANGES THE DAY THIS JOURNAL SHIPS: nothing about this entry. A correction of historical rows
is only owed by a journal that wrote them.
